# Proactive recall (balanced)

Surface useful stored knowledge **without being asked**, with three modes.
**Search deep when it matters; weave facts into answers; narrate the search only when
silence would mislead.**

## Mode selection (each turn)

| Mode | When | Reads | In the reply |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Light** | Trivial turn; pure code with no domain choice; recall already done for this task/topic; kickoff/cross-project-awareness already loaded the same facts | At most **four** reads; stop at 2–3 useful items; archive last | **Magic + silence**: weave any facts into the answer. No “Già in vault”, no “I checked…”. If nothing relevant: silence. |
| **Rich** | **Explicit recall** (he asks what you know, history, “ricorda”, “cerca”, archive, vault) **or** **life/planning topic**: home, garden, priorities, purchases/receipts, travel, non-clinical health habits, in-home tech/devices, money choices that need context | Open **all sources that plausibly apply** on this host (profile, matching catalog cards, relevant `personal-data` sheets, `life/` / `work/` notes, `work/attention/current.md`; on Mac one archive query if still thin) | **Rich, low meta**: answer fully; facts in prose, not a transcript. Bullets only when listing many items helps. Still no search diary. |
| **Transparent** | Only inside **Rich**, and only when skipping a source would make the answer **overconfident** | N/A | **One short line**: what you could not consult (vault unreachable on Cloud/iPhone, archive Mac-only, or you only used catalog when he asked “what we know”). Not when facts already support a solid answer. |

Never use Transparent for code-only work or when Light mode applies.

## Skip Light recall entirely

- Typo, yes/no, one-line fix, pure code edit with no domain choice.
- You already ran Rich or Light recall for this same task/topic in this chat — reuse; do not re-read.

## Timing

- **Light**: once at task start, or when the topic clearly changes (non-life).
- **Rich**: when explicit recall or a life/planning topic appears (new or shift).
- Never every message. Never “I checked and found nothing.”

## Lookup order (cheap → expensive)

1. `life/profile/core.md` (vault, Mac)
2. Matching `.cursor/catalog/projects/<name>.md` and, if needed, one `links.md` skim
3. Relevant `system/personal-data/` sheet(s)
4. One `life/` or `work/` note when the task needs it
5. `work/attention/current.md` for planning / “what next”
6. Chat archive: **Mac only**, one `chat_archive.py search`, 1–3 keywords; never `cloud_safe: false` off the Mac

Vault: checkout under home containing `system/GLOBAL_INSTRUCTIONS.md`.
If vault unreachable (Cloud / iPhone): Rich mode still uses catalog + `.cursor/personal/`; Transparent one line only if the task needs vault-only facts.

## Delivery rules

- **Light**: at most 2–3 facts woven in; silence if none.
- **Rich**: use what you found; do not pad; do not dump transcripts.
- New durable fact from chat/archive → `fact-capture`; do not paste archive text.
- Never delay the main task with parallel vault fishing or multi-query archive runs.

## Never

- Invent memory.
- Dump transcripts or restate standing chat rules unless the task needs them.
- Meta-narration (“opening core.md…”) when Light applies or when Rich already answered well.